<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd">

    <!--
      band-330 — access_suspension role vocabulary: add ROLE_MESH.

      The platform gained a ROLE_MESH access role (the gateway route-access FLOOR for
      /bff/mesh/**, seeded in Casdoor). Every OTHER access role in the platform's
      suspension vocabulary — ROLE_MATRIX, ROLE_MASTODON — can be banned and
      temp-banned through the access_suspension desired-state machinery; ROLE_MESH
      could not, so a mesh abuser could only be handled by an operator manually
      stripping the Casdoor role: no audit row, no expiry clock, no restore path.
      This widens the closed role vocabulary so the SAME ban / timed-suspend /
      auto-restore machinery covers the mesh surface.

      The suspension EFFECT for ROLE_MESH is the Casdoor role-membership drop ALONE
      (MeshAccessSyncAction) — see that class's own doc for why there is deliberately
      no downstream service leg: mesh has no homeserver, so removing the role makes
      every gateway allow-predicate on /bff/mesh/** false, which is
      governed-but-ungranted -> DENY.

      Additive — every value previously allowed is still allowed. Done as a NEW
      changeset rather than editing the immutable 008-access-suspension-role-check
      changeSet, so an already-applied deployment migrates forward cleanly.

      ── Numbering: 330 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      The highest band wired in db.changelog-master.xml today is 320
      (320-service-scaffold, the Service-Store scaffold record); 330 is the next free
      band above it and leaves the customary 10-wide gap for that band to grow into.
      Appended LAST at the include site — access_suspension (008) and its named
      ck_access_suspension_role constraint already exist by here, so the drop +
      re-add applies cleanly.

      ── Portable DDL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      Plain ALTER TABLE … DROP/ADD CONSTRAINT in a <sql> block with a <rollback>
      that restores the exact pre-330 three-value CHECK — the SAME shape
      063-notification-delivery-skipped uses to widen the 062 status CHECK. NOT
      Postgres-gated: unlike the partial indexes and the runtime GRANTs in 008 (both
      dbms=postgresql onFail=MARK_RAN), a named CHECK constraint is portable, so the
      widened vocabulary must apply on EVERY store the changelog runs against — a
      gated version would leave a test/dev store rejecting ROLE_MESH inserts that
      production accepts.
    -->

    <changeSet id="330-access-suspension-role-add-mesh" author="hugmesh">
        <comment>Widen the access_suspension role CHECK to add ROLE_MESH (the
                 /bff/mesh/** access role) alongside ROLE_MATRIX, ROLE_MASTODON and
                 PROFILE. Additive — drops then re-creates the named CHECK with the
                 superset of values. SuspensionRequest / AdminController @Pattern
                 parity.</comment>
        <sql>ALTER TABLE access_suspension DROP CONSTRAINT ck_access_suspension_role</sql>
        <sql>
            ALTER TABLE access_suspension
                ADD CONSTRAINT ck_access_suspension_role
                CHECK (role IN ('ROLE_MATRIX', 'ROLE_MASTODON', 'ROLE_MESH', 'PROFILE'))
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            ALTER TABLE access_suspension DROP CONSTRAINT ck_access_suspension_role;
            ALTER TABLE access_suspension
                ADD CONSTRAINT ck_access_suspension_role
                CHECK (role IN ('ROLE_MATRIX', 'ROLE_MASTODON', 'PROFILE'))
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
